    "updated_at": "2024-02-14T06:28:17Z",
    "body": "The WebSocket `close()` method can already be used to do this. If you don't like Chrome's behaviour of printing a console message when this happens you should file an issue at https://crbug.com/.\r\n\r\nThe [proposed WebSocketStream API](https://github.com/whatwg/websockets/pull/48) uses AbortController for cancelling the handshake already.\r\n\r\nWe are unlikely to add this to the WebSocket API because it can be easily emulated with a function like\r\n\r\n```js\r\nfunction AbortableWebSocket(url, signal) {\r\n  signal.throwIfAborted();\r\n  const ws = new WebSocket(url);\r\n  const abortHandler = () => ws.close();\r\n  signal.addEventListener('abort', abortHandler);\r\n  ws.addEventListener('open', \r\n    () => signal.removeEventListener('abort', abortHandler));\r\n  return ws;\r\n}\r\n```",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
